operator-session.raw is the byte stream ssh printed (CR LF line ends);
operator-session.txt is the same with CR removed. raw sha256
c4198547a5fa142db72d7d43e86c749233088ef733559285b2e4b506d6286f58

An earlier session on the first boot of the same image ran the list
without `cd /home/operator`: the shell starts in /, which sessions see
read-only, so `echo hello > notes.txt` printed
"absd-sh: /notes.txt: not found" and `cat notes.txt` printed
"cat: notes.txt: ABSD path not found". That run is why `cd` is in the
input above.
